WEBVTT

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:03.200
This girl is Kouyama Mitsuki. 12 years old.

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:05.810
The long-awaited day of <i>Full Moon's</i> debut has finally arrived.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.770
But, at her first live performance...

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:11.220
She was nervous because she had to sing in front of so many people.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:13.280
It's to be expected... she's still a grade school student, after all.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:14.230
However...

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:15.410
Thanks to everyone's help...{}

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:16.700
It's safe to say that the debut was a success. {It's fine by me}

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:19.990
Next time, I'm going to be the one to debut as <i>Full Moon.</i>

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.070
Well, then...

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:22.870
...I wonder what's going to happen today.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:23.450
Huh?

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:28.820
Do you understand?

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:29.670
Yes.

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:28.700
<i>Full Moon.</i>

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:29.370
<i>Myself.</i>

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:31.450
<i>In stores now.</i>  {In clear engrish}

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:34.580
It's so pretty...!

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:36.790
Is this... really me?

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:40.540
For one of Seed Records' new artists...

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:43.760
...they put in a little extra for the TV ad.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:46.300
But... I wonder if everyone will really buy it...

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:49.680
Losing confidence in your first sales attempt is a problem.

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:52.040
There's no mistake... it's a good song.

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:54.520
It's going to be a smashing success!

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:04.820
Ah... man!

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:06.900
Just calm down... calm down!

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:09.780
Until I hear about the sales from Ooshige-san...

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:12.260
...I can't calm down.

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:14.540
Man... give me a break.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:17.080
Hurry up and call, Manager!

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:18.370
It's here!

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:22.340
Hello?

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:23.210
Yes.

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:24.340
Is that so?

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:25.630
I understand.

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:30.510
How...

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:31.010
...did it go? {continuation of Meroko from Takuto}

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:36.130
Um... that's... uh...

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:38.190
Maybe it's a slow seller.

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:40.380
It only stared selling yesterday, right?

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:42.350
We've only begun the fight, right?

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:44.940
All right!

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:46.360
It's a smashing hit!

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:49.840
They're receiving orders...

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:51.580
...the sales are still going!

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:52.810
What's that...

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:54.720
...you had us worried...

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:55.700
This means that...

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:58.960
...lots of people are going to 
hear my song, right?

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:01.040
If you had my cunning...

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:02.820
...you'd sell even more.

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:04.840
A <i>million seller</i>... without a doubt!

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:07.300
I'm so happy!

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:09.910
Isn't it great..?{}

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:12.030
After today...

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:15.410
...talk about <i>Full Moon</i>  will be everywhere.

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:16.350
That's right!

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:19.020
You should take your CD to school today!

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:20.140
Eh?!

00:04:20.770 --> 00:04:23.980
You can brag and say, "I have <i>Full Moon's</i>  CD!"

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:24.860
Maybe...

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:26.360
It'd be nice if I could do that...

00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:28.490
Everyone will want it!

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:31.110
Ah. If that's going to happen, then I should practice my signature first.

00:04:31.610 --> 00:04:32.820
You know...

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:35.450
The one who's selling isn't you, it's <i>Full Moon...</i>

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:38.830
Do you think a ribbon would make me look cuter? {Shani: actually she is talking about her signature here and not herself, so it should be "it" instead of "me", oh well, I guess it will create confusion, so I am leaving it as is.}

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:40.580
Hey... what do you think?

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:43.670
Meroko, cut it out already...

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:49.970
Such unladylike behavior...

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:50.840
Good morning! {Do I have to put with timing all these "Good Mornings", ugh}

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:51.010
Good morning! {Do I have to put all these "Good Mornings", ugh}

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:51.800
Good morning! {Do I have to put all these "Good Mornings", ugh}

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:52.760
Good morning!

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:08.070
What is it?

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:10.940
I'm thinking about what they all might say...

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:12.340
My heart's pounding.

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:16.030
I wonder if they really heard <i>Myself...</i>{going crazy over sales results! :D}

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:17.990
It's fine. After all...

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:19.560
...it was a smashing hit, right?

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:20.790
Have some faith in yourself.

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:21.710
That's right.

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:22.830
Try taking a deep breath. {Takuto no Aho! He forgot to tell her to write hito on her palm :|}

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:29.740
It looks like... I've calmed down a bit.

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:30.670
Then, you're ready.

00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:31.090
Yep!

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:33.590
Good morning!

00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:34.430
Ah...

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:36.010
Good morning, Kouyama-san!

00:05:36.010 --> 00:05:36.850
Good morning!

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:38.930
And... just earlier...

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:41.300
Morning, Kumi!

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:42.600
Geez, Kumi.

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:44.280
You're in a hurry today.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:45.270
Whatever...

00:05:45.270 --> 00:05:48.730
Anyways, did you hear the new single that came out yesterday?

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:51.110
I heard it. I heard it!

00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:52.990
The vocal for it was the best! {Vocals?}

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:54.070
Um...

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:55.280
<i>Fu...</i>

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:00.620
It's <i>Full Moon</i>.

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:02.250
Furuta!

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:04.250
From the <i>Guitar Fighters?</i>

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:05.460
That's it!

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:07.460
Maijima-san sure knows 
what she's talking about.

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:09.380
Of course!

00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:10.980
I keep up to date on all the new songs.

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:12.160
Really, Chia-san?

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:13.690
What's she doing?

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:15.260
She's supposed to go tell them...

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:15.880
Yeah.

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:20.000
Hey, on TV yesterday...

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:23.630
I was so surprised... she was so pretty...

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:26.190
You're talking about 
the entertainment news, right?

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:36.820
What's wrong, Kouyama-san?

00:06:36.820 --> 00:06:39.030
Are you feeling sick again?

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:41.310
I-It's nothing.

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:42.990
Thanks.

00:06:43.370 --> 00:06:44.000
Really.

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:45.960
That's good, I guess...

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:01.100
Nobody's talking about me at all...

00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:05.770
If you're that concerned about it...

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:07.480
Don't bother yourself with gossip.

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:09.770
Why don't you try asking someone yourself?

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:12.020
Because...

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:14.530
It couldn't be that... 
you don't have any friends?

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:18.130
Of course not!

00:07:18.130 --> 00:07:20.450
It's been two years since 
she transferred here.

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:23.240
It's just as Takuto said.

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:26.790
I've been absent a lot due to my illness, after all.

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:30.720
My health has only been getting worse...

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:33.280
...and I am not allowed to watch 
TV much either, so... {"such unladylike behavior! Wanting to watch tv!" Poor Girl. T_T}{rephrased}

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:34.810
...I don't have anything to talk about.

00:07:34.810 --> 00:07:37.880
That's why... I've never been able to make close friends.

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:40.090
I see...

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:40.970
Sorry...

00:07:42.220 --> 00:07:42.780
It's okay.

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:44.880
As long as I'm selling...

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:46.730
Everyone will be listening to me...

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:48.560
...so I can't just dwell in the past.

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:51.400
I'm sorry, too, for making you worry.

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:56.320
Geez...

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:08.250
Uh... Ah...?

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:10.480
Ah?

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:13.790
Ah! This is it!

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:15.880
Wh-What's with you all of a sudden?

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:16.760
Look at this!

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:19.000
{NO TS?}

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:19.000
Lunchtime broadcast inside the school.

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:20.800
Taking song requests?{edited}

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:21.760
What's this?

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:23.380
During our lunch break...

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:25.030
We have a broadcast DJ...

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:27.640
A lot of songs are played, and there's a lot of talking, too.

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:30.230
It's pretty popular.

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:31.230
Like I said...

00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:31.980
That's it!

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:32.400
Eh?

00:08:33.230 --> 00:08:35.110
Geez... you're so slow...

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:36.610
If nobody's heard you before...

00:08:36.610 --> 00:08:38.690
...then we'll let them hear you.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:40.950
Eh?!!!

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:42.530
That's what we'll do.

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:45.780
It's okay if we broadcast your CD, right?

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.740
I guess so...

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:49.290
But...

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:50.400
Ah! Geez!

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:51.580
You're so frustrating!

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:54.750
...you'll never make it in the market.

00:08:55.050 --> 00:08:56.800
It's easy to give up, but...

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:59.210
...try working a little harder first!

00:08:59.210 --> 00:09:00.300
He's right.

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:02.180
You finally managed to debut.

00:09:06.220 --> 00:09:07.320
That's right...

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:09.180
Maybe I should try working a little harder...

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:10.810
It's not <i>"maybe I should try..."</i>

00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:12.960
It's "I'm gonna work hard!"

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:14.030
Wait a minute!

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:17.770
I haven't even thought about whether or not to request it!

00:09:17.770 --> 00:09:19.360
You're still saying that?!

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:20.570
If that's the case...

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:27.910
Mero Mero Magic!

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:33.120
Ah.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:34.290
My CD...

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:37.090
I'm going to request this!

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:38.670
Meroko, wait!

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:39.800
You idiot!

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:42.670
I said wait up!

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:45.800
Please wait!

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:48.300
Look... isn't that Kouyama-san?

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:49.880
What's with her?

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:50.960
What a weird girl.

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:52.230
She's so strange.

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:54.280
Ah... th-thanks...

00:09:57.910 --> 00:10:00.230
She's done it now... that Meroko...

00:10:00.230 --> 00:10:02.110
Meroko, geez!

00:10:02.110 --> 00:10:03.400
Stop!

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:05.490
Stop already, Meroko!

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:09.080
That's the broadcasting room isn't it?

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:17.960
Don't just suddenly stop!

00:10:18.170 --> 00:10:18.710
Huh?

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:22.510
Kouyama-san... why are you down there?

00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:24.630
Ma-Maijima-san!{}

00:10:24.630 --> 00:10:25.510
Okay?

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:26.890
For the broadcast...

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:29.240
Say, "I want to request this", 'kay?

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:30.470
Oh well...

00:10:30.470 --> 00:10:32.270
If it's come to this... just give in.

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:33.680
Are you okay?

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:35.230
Ah... um...

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:36.600
That...

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:38.270
Um...

00:10:38.270 --> 00:10:39.310
Well...

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:41.150
Ah... geez!

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:43.650
No!

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:45.320
What?

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:47.160
Just hush, 'kay?

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:49.070
Play <i>Myself!</i>

00:10:49.070 --> 00:10:49.950
I mean...

00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:52.580
Please play<i> Myself.</i>

00:10:52.580 --> 00:10:53.120
'kay?

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:53.660
'kay?

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:54.370
It's okay, right?

00:10:54.370 --> 00:10:54.830
'kay?

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:56.970
Huh?

00:10:56.970 --> 00:10:59.040
I wonder what Kouyama-san's doing...

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:01.500
Is she fighting with Maijima-san?

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:03.630
Cut it out, Meroko!

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:05.670
It's because you have to request it!

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:11.460
Um...

00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:13.930
Kouyama-san... just what was that?

00:11:15.770 --> 00:11:16.810
I'm very sorry!

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:21.730
Oh man...

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:25.320
Kouyama-san?

00:11:25.320 --> 00:11:26.070
Are you okay?

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:29.470
Only strange things are happening to me...

00:11:29.470 --> 00:11:33.030
I can't take it anymore...

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:52.300
Ah...

00:11:52.300 --> 00:11:54.270
I didn't give her the CD...

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:55.520
Nothing's changed...

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:56.640
This sucks...

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:58.020
You said it...

00:11:58.020 --> 00:12:00.020
Who's fault do you think it is?

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:01.200
Ah?

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:03.920
Maijima-san.

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:06.360
This is your chance.

00:12:06.610 --> 00:12:10.050
This is your chance, so go 
and try requesting again!

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:11.570
I wonder if it is...

00:12:11.570 --> 00:12:12.660
Of course it is!

00:12:12.660 --> 00:12:14.390
Ah......

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:15.490
Ah...

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:17.600
Um... Maijima-san...{name correction}

00:12:20.790 --> 00:12:21.170
Yes.

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:21.920
Hello?

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:23.040
You know...

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:26.310
Maybe she was buying<i> Myself?</i>

00:12:26.590 --> 00:12:30.550
Don't just stand there 
and say irresponsible things!

00:12:30.550 --> 00:12:32.490
Because, look at that.

00:12:38.810 --> 00:12:39.600
Ah.

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:40.530
<i>Myself?</i>

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:41.480
<i>Full Moon's?</i>

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:42.980
See!

00:12:43.270 --> 00:12:44.530
Absolutely...

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:45.440
...hopeless.{}

00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:46.150
Eh?

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:48.550
Yep, Yep.

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:50.140
By the way...

00:12:50.140 --> 00:12:52.370
I'm going with my mother to Shibuya tomorrow.

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:53.570
I'm looking forward to it.

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:55.000
<i>"Hopeless..."</i>{edited for continuation}

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:56.410
What does she mean?

00:13:02.120 --> 00:13:03.540
I'm home.

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:08.420
Well...

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:10.450
How did you get that injury?

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:12.180
This is...

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:16.910
Lately, you've...

00:13:16.910 --> 00:13:20.140
...been joking around and acting rather flippant, you know.{edited}

00:13:22.140 --> 00:13:24.000
You have to consider your health, so...

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:25.610
...be more careful from now on.

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:27.210
Do you understand?

00:13:28.880 --> 00:13:29.610
Yes...

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:38.010
Wow!

00:13:38.010 --> 00:13:39.160
This taiyaki...!

00:13:39.160 --> 00:13:40.370
It's <i>sooo</i>  good!

00:13:40.370 --> 00:13:41.120
Come on! Come on!

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:42.370
It smells good, doesn't it?

00:13:42.370 --> 00:13:42.910
Well? Well? Well?

00:13:42.910 --> 00:13:43.580
Look!

00:13:43.580 --> 00:13:44.460
I don't want any.

00:13:44.790 --> 00:13:46.290
What are you saying?!

00:13:46.290 --> 00:13:48.290
The tail is filled with anko...

00:13:48.290 --> 00:13:50.550
It's refreshing.

00:13:50.630 --> 00:13:51.130
That's right!

00:13:51.130 --> 00:13:53.340
You'll regret it if you don't have any!

00:13:53.340 --> 00:13:53.930
Come on! Come on!

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:54.510
Come on! Come on!

00:13:54.550 --> 00:13:55.050
Well?

00:13:55.050 --> 00:13:55.840
Well? Well? Well?

00:13:55.840 --> 00:13:56.640
Well?

00:13:55.840 --> 00:13:56.640
Well?

00:13:55.840 --> 00:13:56.640
Geez!

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:58.550
I don't want any means I don't want any!

00:13:58.760 --> 00:13:59.220
Ah?

00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:06.900
Yes?

00:14:07.690 --> 00:14:09.030
Ah. Mitsuki?

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:10.010
It's Ooshige.

00:14:10.610 --> 00:14:13.320
There's already a huge response for<i> Myself.</i>

00:14:13.780 --> 00:14:16.650
The CD shop has already sent additional orders.

00:14:16.650 --> 00:14:20.290
It's the first time one of my talents
 has been such a huge hit!{line break}

00:14:20.870 --> 00:14:22.160
You said it's a hit, but...

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:23.790
...is it really?

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:25.680
Of course!

00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:29.170
The radio and television stations want an interview as soon as possible.

00:14:29.170 --> 00:14:30.840
They've all been asking for one.

00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:31.500
Can you hear it?

00:14:31.500 --> 00:14:33.760
All the phones here are going off.

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:35.220
Is that so?

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:37.760
But... nobody knows about it...

00:14:37.760 --> 00:14:38.090
Eh?

00:14:38.260 --> 00:14:38.970
Mitsuki?

00:14:38.970 --> 00:14:39.760
Hello?

00:14:39.970 --> 00:14:40.640
Mitsuki?

00:14:41.850 --> 00:14:42.720
Excuse me.

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:48.690
Your manager is going to worry about you.

00:14:48.940 --> 00:14:49.650
Because...!

00:14:49.650 --> 00:14:51.090
Even though nobody's heard it...

00:14:51.090 --> 00:14:52.900
...why does she say it's a hit?!

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:54.370
That's because...

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:57.110
But... there hasn't been 
much publicity for it...

00:14:57.110 --> 00:14:59.630
Even if there was publicity, 
no one would listen to it!

00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:01.000
It's useless!

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:02.370
Besides...

00:15:12.630 --> 00:15:13.300
Sorry.

00:15:13.890 --> 00:15:16.260
Can you leave me alone for a bit?

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:19.390
Don't come to school anymore either.

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:26.310
I'm leaving.

00:15:32.270 --> 00:15:33.980
Good morning!

00:15:33.980 --> 00:15:34.690
Good morning!

00:15:41.450 --> 00:15:43.490
For some reason... I don't think I'll make it...

00:15:43.740 --> 00:15:45.500
What are you saying after coming this far?

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:48.840
Takuto!

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:49.620
Ah.

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:51.710
I'm sorry about yesterday.

00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:52.670
It's okay.

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:55.280
Anyways, don't get hung up over something like that.

00:15:55.280 --> 00:15:57.170
You can't act like before from now on.

00:15:57.550 --> 00:15:58.420
That's because...

00:15:58.420 --> 00:16:01.610
I thought everyone would be 
talking about <i>Full Moon!</i>

00:16:01.610 --> 00:16:04.140
Yet everyone... Even after
 I put all I had into it...{edited}

00:16:04.430 --> 00:16:05.530
You know...{}

00:16:05.530 --> 00:16:08.640
If you want them to hear you sing, then sing for them yourself!

00:16:08.640 --> 00:16:10.210
You want to be friends with them after all!{edited}

00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:12.440
If you don't tell them yourself...

00:16:12.440 --> 00:16:14.360
...they won't be your friends.

00:16:15.480 --> 00:16:17.070
Sing together?

00:16:17.320 --> 00:16:18.770
Like I said...

00:16:18.950 --> 00:16:20.780
The fact that you don't have 
any girls you're close to.

00:16:20.780 --> 00:16:22.740
Before you can even start worrying about how you can't talk to anyone...

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:25.970
Smile and try to talk to them yourself first!

00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:28.010
I see...

00:16:28.330 --> 00:16:29.710
Sing together, huh?

00:16:30.020 --> 00:16:30.820
That's right.

00:16:30.820 --> 00:16:32.210
Anyways, give it a try.{edited}

00:16:32.520 --> 00:16:34.290
I wonder if I can do it.

00:16:34.290 --> 00:16:35.440
I told you yesterday, right?

00:16:35.440 --> 00:16:37.010
In times like this...

00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:43.140
That's right.

00:16:43.640 --> 00:16:45.260
I should smile myself.

00:16:46.390 --> 00:16:47.350
Come. Come. {Oh no she didn't}

00:16:47.350 --> 00:16:49.410
Check this out. Look at this.

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:51.010
That voice is...

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:55.190
What we have here is...

00:16:55.190 --> 00:16:58.610
It just went on sale yesterday... {Oh yes she did}{Shani: Meroko is so damn awesome!}

00:16:58.780 --> 00:16:59.610
Right now...

00:16:59.610 --> 00:17:01.570
There's a mad rush to acquire this huge hit...

00:17:01.570 --> 00:17:02.570
It's crazy! {Kwayzyyyyyy}

00:17:02.570 --> 00:17:03.410
Which means...

00:17:03.410 --> 00:17:06.080
It's something you can't easily get! {Is it drugs?}

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:07.000
Over here...

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:10.460
Don't just sit there studying 
with your buddies...

00:17:12.100 --> 00:17:13.000
Come!

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:14.380
Buy it! Buy it!

00:17:15.550 --> 00:17:17.420
Those are... my CDs...{edited}{copyright infringement :D}

00:17:17.420 --> 00:17:19.160
What the hell is she doing?

00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:21.840
Kouyama-san somehow become quite a character all of a sudden.

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:24.760
I never thought she was 
this kind of a person. {edited}

00:17:25.050 --> 00:17:25.550
Yeah.

00:17:25.550 --> 00:17:28.020
It's totally different from her image.

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:28.930
You're horrible...

00:17:29.070 --> 00:17:30.680
You're horrible, Meroko! {Shani: WHOA! I almost feared she gave it away that Meroko was her double there, mattaku mo...}

00:17:34.480 --> 00:17:36.210
What were you thinking? {For shame}

00:17:36.650 --> 00:17:37.860
Because...

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:42.160
I thought I was kinda wrong yesterday...

00:17:42.530 --> 00:17:44.050
If you're regretting it...

00:17:44.050 --> 00:17:46.240
Why did you pretend to be her?

00:17:46.240 --> 00:17:48.730
If they listen to <i>Full Moon's</i>  song...

00:17:48.730 --> 00:17:52.410
...Mitsuki will be able to make lots of friends, won't she?

00:17:52.810 --> 00:17:55.680
Even if that was your goal, 
your methods were wrong!{edited}

00:17:56.010 --> 00:17:58.920
I thought that was the best way 
to get their attention.

00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:00.000
You know...

00:18:00.640 --> 00:18:02.120
It's okay, Takuto.

00:18:02.630 --> 00:18:03.040
Eh?

00:18:03.890 --> 00:18:04.740
That's enough...

00:18:05.010 --> 00:18:05.470
Well...

00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:08.640
Meroko was doing it for my sake, too.

00:18:09.890 --> 00:18:10.560
Besides...

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:12.480
I didn't have friends to begin with, so...

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:15.320
It won't change the way people think about me.

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:15.730
Ah...

00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:19.480
I have to go already.

00:18:28.950 --> 00:18:31.370
I thought it was a good idea...

00:18:31.370 --> 00:18:31.840
Hmm?

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:36.920
Ah... she's here! She's here!

00:18:37.170 --> 00:18:39.340
Man... we were looking all over
 for you, Kouyama-san.

00:18:39.730 --> 00:18:40.040
Eh?

00:18:42.920 --> 00:18:47.010
Hey, I was wondering if it's okay for me to use this CD during the lunchtime broadcast.

00:18:47.300 --> 00:18:48.040
Eh?!

00:18:48.040 --> 00:18:48.800
But...

00:18:48.800 --> 00:18:52.010
You said it was absolutely hopeless yesterday.

00:18:52.310 --> 00:18:53.370
That's right.

00:18:53.370 --> 00:18:56.690
No matter where I went... 
I couldn't get one at all.

00:18:56.920 --> 00:19:00.190
I was even thinking that I'd have to go to Shibuya to find a copy...

00:19:00.190 --> 00:19:01.620
It's really popular.

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:02.770
The lyrics are great...

00:19:02.770 --> 00:19:04.490
The song's the best!

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:05.580
Especially that part.

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:08.660
Doushite konna ni...

00:19:08.660 --> 00:19:10.340
No, you're wrong.

00:19:10.340 --> 00:19:12.830
Doushite konna ni...

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:14.200
That seems kinda off.

00:19:14.200 --> 00:19:15.040
Really?

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:16.620
I'm pretty sure it went like this...

00:19:16.620 --> 00:19:19.720
Doushite konna ni...

00:19:21.270 --> 00:19:22.370
You think so?

00:19:24.350 --> 00:19:25.870
If I recall...

00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:28.630
Um... um...

00:19:29.720 --> 00:19:30.670
Isn't it like this?

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:56.620
Ah sorry.

00:19:56.620 --> 00:19:57.690
I shouldn't have done that.

00:19:58.710 --> 00:19:59.540
Amazing.

00:19:59.540 --> 00:20:01.330
Kouyama-san, you're like the real thing.

00:20:01.330 --> 00:20:02.270
You're so cool!

00:20:02.270 --> 00:20:02.630
Eh?

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:03.630
I wonder if that's so...

00:20:03.860 --> 00:20:04.400
Yeah.

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:06.680
Kouyama-san, you're good at singing, aren't you?

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:08.220
It's not just singing...

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:09.560
Her performance earlier.

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:11.590
Ah... That was hilarious.

00:20:11.590 --> 00:20:12.930
Ah... that was...

00:20:14.930 --> 00:20:16.850
Hang out with us more from now on, okay?

00:20:17.100 --> 00:20:18.100
Teach us how to sing, too.

00:20:19.190 --> 00:20:19.560
Okay!

00:20:19.940 --> 00:20:21.520
If I can do it, I'll sing as much as you want!

00:20:21.770 --> 00:20:22.650
Hey, Mitsuki...

00:20:22.670 --> 00:20:24.730
Ah! It's okay if we call you Mitsuki, right?

00:20:24.730 --> 00:20:26.290
Do you want to come to 
the broadcast with me?{line break}

00:20:26.290 --> 00:20:28.360
I'll show you how it's done... 
broadcasting, that is...{line break}

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:30.070
Okay!

00:20:30.070 --> 00:20:30.960
I want to try it!

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:33.570
You can call me Tomoe.

00:20:35.030 --> 00:20:35.780
Well, well.

00:20:35.780 --> 00:20:38.040
That takes care of this for now.

00:20:39.710 --> 00:20:40.500
Meroko.

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:42.170
I'm sorry for saying mean things to you.

00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:43.670
Takuto, thank you.

00:20:43.670 --> 00:20:44.340
Mitsuki.

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:45.170
What's wrong?

00:20:45.170 --> 00:20:46.480
Oh, I'm coming right away. {she is talking with her friends here}

00:20:46.480 --> 00:20:46.990
Bye! {and this one is with the Negi Ramen}

00:20:49.760 --> 00:20:50.400
All right!

00:20:50.400 --> 00:20:51.840
Thanks to what I did...

00:20:51.840 --> 00:20:55.300
I don't have to leave, and <i>Full Moon</i>  won't be sad anymore, right, Takuto? {double space added between "Full Moon" and "won't"}

00:20:55.300 --> 00:20:56.640
You're getting better.

00:21:01.390 --> 00:21:02.320
Look at this.

00:21:02.810 --> 00:21:04.660
It's really selling.

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:06.500
The production can't even keep up with it.

00:21:06.500 --> 00:21:08.720
Everyone wants to listen to <i>Full Moon's</i>  song!

00:21:08.720 --> 00:21:09.780
Believe me! {Believe it!, Oh how I wanted to use this line.}

00:21:10.320 --> 00:21:10.830
Yes.{edited}

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:11.740
I know.

00:21:11.990 --> 00:21:13.250
Like I said...!

00:21:13.640 --> 00:21:14.040
Eh?

00:21:14.700 --> 00:21:16.200
I know it very well.

00:21:16.200 --> 00:21:18.370
Lots of people are listening to it.

00:21:18.920 --> 00:21:20.580
From now on, I'll work harder!{edited}

00:21:22.580 --> 00:21:24.400
Take a deep breath and smile!

00:21:27.670 --> 00:21:29.000
Oh well.

00:23:07.560 --> 00:23:08.600
Hmm...

00:23:09.860 --> 00:23:11.360
That doctor, Wakaouji...{edited}

00:23:11.360 --> 00:23:12.690
What's on his mind?

00:23:12.940 --> 00:23:14.490
No matter how many times he goes around with Mitsuki...

00:23:14.490 --> 00:23:16.280
He hasn't heard of <i>Myself.</i>

00:23:16.280 --> 00:23:17.490
Eh? Why?

00:23:17.490 --> 00:23:18.820
It's a good song...

00:23:19.850 --> 00:23:21.120
Now that you mention it... that person...

00:23:21.120 --> 00:23:23.330
Someone said he was 
a musician before, right?

00:23:23.580 --> 00:23:25.370
Is there something else to him?

00:23:25.910 --> 00:23:27.670
Next time on Full Moon wo Sagashite:

00:23:27.910 --> 00:23:29.170
I Wanted You to Listen{changed as instructed in episode 09}
